OL,3,GNEWSA'I'm glad my stroke happened, I
OL,4,Awouldn't change it'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA dad-of-two who suffered a
OL,7,Flife-changing stroke last year has said
OL,8,Fhe is glad that it happened.
OL,10,FTim Jacobs, from Worcester, was left
OL,11,Funable to walk or speak following a
OL,12,Fhaemorrhagic stroke, also known as a
OL,13,Fbleed on the brain.
OL,15,FThe 40-year-old, originally from the
OL,16,FNetherlands, added that prior to his
OL,17,Fstroke, he had always struggled with
OL,18,Fanxiety and depression, which he
OL,19,Fdescribed as "on and off".
